build: 2026-06-23 v10.59.0 (rPPG lock fix + audited hot-loop optimizations)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notes: Consolidated build. (1) rPPG LOCK FIX (v10.58 carried forward): the fresh-lock gate in CameraAnalyzer no longer DISCARDS a window when peak-counting disagrees with a confident autocorrelation — it now SEEDS the BPM from the robust autocorrelation period instead (root cause of "finger=yes, q≈0.30, bpm=0 forever" on device). Stage telemetry added to the breadcrumb (amp/pk/acf) to pinpoint any remaining weak-signal case. (2) OPTIMIZE-ALL PASS: ran a 3-agent audit (audio-thread, app performance, code quality). Findings: the audio render path is exemplary (pre-allocated buffers, lock-free SPSC, vDSP, no violations) and the codebase is crash-clean (no force-unwraps, all divisions/subscripts guarded). Landed only the clearly-safe, output-preserving, compile-verified wins in the live ~15 Hz rPPG loop: CameraAnalyzer finger detection now uses an O(1) running true-count instead of a per-frame filter{}.count allocation (both analysis paths), and recentWaveform uses vDSP_maxmgv to drop an intermediate abs-array allocation on its ~10 Hz read — less main-actor allocation churn while the camera path is live. DEFERRED as device-gated (behaviour/structure changes that must be verified on hardware, not shipped blind): EngineBus per-frame Task→direct main-actor setter, splitting the large EchoelStudioView body to cut bio-rate re-renders, RespirationEstimator incremental ingest, and in-place DMX (Art-Net/sACN) packet buffers. PulsePeriodEstimator and the protected Rausch triad untouched. iOS compile gate validates; ci.yml runs the pure tests.
